@@ -141,6 +141,22 @@ ## Authorization boundary
 
 Do not rely on hidden UI controls as authorization.
 
+## Tenant session
+
+A signed-in user works in one entity at a time. The choice lives in the session
+under `current_entity_id`, and only the HTTP layer reads it:
+
+- The `current_entity` route middleware resolves the session entity into the
+  request's tenant context (`App\Tenancy\CurrentEntity`). A user who is not a
+  member of that entity gets 403.
+- With no session entity, the middleware (and `/home`) decides: no membership
+  goes to onboarding, exactly one membership is selected, and several go to the
+  switcher (`entity.switcher`).
+- `POST /e/{entity:slug}/pick` is the only way to change the session entity. It
+  checks membership before it writes the session and records an audit line.
+- Domain code (actions, policies, models) receives the entity as an argument and
+  never reads the session.
+
 ## Source of truth
 
